# The coefficient prime selected by a p-adic embedding is maximal

Theorem statement: `MTT.Eigenform.coefficientPrime_isMaximal`
(`50aa5bf2-15e7-4738-b986-9b482f3505e6`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20.

Proof: submission `1334ed49-8e51-4902-9e52-f65f6daebd7d`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-20 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

For an eigenform of positive level and weight at least two, the
nonzero prime ideal of its coefficient ring selected by a $p$-adic embedding
is maximal.

## Explanation of the source proof

The coefficient field is a number field by the previously proved finite-dimensionality theorem. Its
integer ring is therefore a Dedekind domain. Apply `Ideal.IsPrime.isMaximal` to
`coefficientPrime_isPrime`, using `coefficientPrime_ne_bot`, which in turn follows from
`p_mem_coefficientPrime`. The uploaded theorem is at `_root_.solution`.

<!-- Generated by add_prove2me_provenance.py -->
-/

section privateSection

noncomputable section

theorem solution
    {N k p : ℕ} (hN : 0 < N) (hk : 2 ≤ k)
    {ι : MTT.Qbar →+* ℂ} [Fact p.Prime]
    (f : MTT.Eigenform N k ι) (ιp : MTT.Qbar →+* ℂ_[p]) :
    (f.coefficientPrime ιp).IsMaximal := by
  let _ := MTT.numberField_coefficientField hN hk ι f
  exact (f.coefficientPrime_isPrime ιp).isMaximal
    (f.coefficientPrime_ne_bot ιp)
end

end privateSection

